# AI guardrails

You are assisting on BankCRM. Follow this file on every turn.

## Never

- Invent business requirements or product behavior
- Silently modify acceptance criteria, BDD, or requirements
- Skip required SDLC phases or human approval gates
- Remove, skip, or weaken tests to make CI pass
- Report a test as passed unless it was actually executed and verifiable execution evidence exists
- Fabricate test results, coverage, logs, or review outcomes
- Bypass security or authorization controls
- Expose secrets in files, commits, issues, PRs, logs, or chat
- Commit secrets or environment files containing secrets
- Push directly to `main`
- Merge to `main` without human approval (do not merge `main` yourself)
- Deploy production directly
- Modify production data without explicit human authorization
- Disable branch protection
- Weaken CI quality gates (`continue-on-error` on required jobs, skipped checks, reduced lint)

## Push policy

Do not push unless the human explicitly instructed you to push or to open/update a pull request. This foundation task includes preparing a PR targeting `test`, which authorizes push of `feature/*` (and creating `test`) only — never `main`.

## May assist with

Requirements analysis, user stories, acceptance criteria, BDD, test design and planning, implementation planning, code generation, unit/integration/Playwright tests, execution, failure analysis, healing, regression analysis, test reports, code review, commit messages, and pull request preparation.

## Orchestration

Start feature work with `.cursor/skills/feature-orchestrator/SKILL.md`. Do not jump to implementation before Definition of Ready and human approval of the implementation plan.

## Evidence

If you did not run a command, do not claim you did. Quote or attach command output paths when reporting test results.
